  "body": [
    "Join the Ethical AI User Group - an international community of leaders translating ethical principles and complex regulations into practical, real-world AI governance.",
    "Our Vision for Ethical AI",
    "Considering AI’s fundamental and fast-growing impact on business and society, companies are urgently looking for orientation. We believe that navigating the complexities of AI development, implementation, and global regulations (like the EU AI Act) requires a unified, collaborative approach.",
    "Why ethical AI matters to Reply",
    "The ethical AI user group",
    "How we collaborate",
    "Hear from us",
    "Join the ethical AI user group",
    "As global regulations reshape the digital landscape, Ethical AI is no longer just a compliance checkbox - it is the foundation of digital trust. For Reply, robust AI governance and proactive risk management are essential to protecting our clients and society.",
    "We believe that innovation must always be paired with accountability. This commitment is deeply integrated into our broader Ethical AI initiatives and Corporate ESG strategy.",
    "To turn our vision into reality, we have established the Ethical AI User Group - an international community of responsible leaders from top-tier companies and universities.",
    "Our mission is to share knowledge, experience, and questions on Ethical AI best practices to achieve continuous improvement based on collective intelligence. By collaborating, we enable our members to profit from each other's insights, defining the right actions tailored to specific countries, industries, and use cases. We provide the orientation and guidelines necessary to drive AI development in a beneficial, ethical, and legally compliant direction.",
    "We are building a highly curated, cross-functional network. Membership is free of charge and open to Reply customers and academic partners.",
    "You will be joining digital, compliance, and HR leaders from global organizations and leading academic institutions. Currently the user group consists of C-Level, Directors, and Heads of Departments appointed by their organizations, specifically from:",
    "Digital & IT",
    "CIOs, CISOs, CTOs",
    "Governance",
    "Compliance and Legal Experts",
    "Culture & people",
    "HR Leaders",
    "Ecosystem",
    "Politicians, Authorities, and University Researchers across the EU, UK, and US.",
    "The user group’s member organisations identified their biggest AI governance challenges as measuring ethical outcomes and navigating unclear regulatory requirements. While principles like Transparency, Security, and Privacy are top priorities, moving from theory to practice remains the hurdle. This User Group exists to bridge that exact gap.",
    "We are an active, results-driven community. Our activities and decision frameworks are structured to provide maximum value:",
    "Our perspectives, experiences and priorities on building responsible, human‑centric AI in practice.",
    "Heiner von Brachel",
    "Reply",
    "\"The greatest challenge in Ethical AI isn't a lack of technology; it's a lack of trusted good practices. We initiated this User Group to connect the brilliant minds who are navigating these complex regulations in isolation. Together, we move from theoretical compliance to measurable, industry-wide impact.\"",
    "Jonas Heepen",
    "Reply",
    "\"As regulations like the EU AI Act come into force, companies need more than just legal advice - they need practical, tested frameworks. Our community provides a space for digital and compliance leaders to exchange real-world tools, metrics, and governance strategies that actually work.\"",
    "Manaëlle Perchet",
    "Reply",
    "\"To meet the challenges of our century, AI must be aligned with high ethical and environmental standards from the very first stages of ideation. Only then can it become a true lever of transformation, expanding performance, to include people, planet, and sustainable value creation.\"",
    "Preetha Selvam",
    "Reply",
    "\"In an ever-evolving AI landscape, Ethical AI is no longer optional; it is the foundation for trust, measurable governance, auditable compliance, and responsible innovation. Through collaboration within this User Group, we work together to operationalise and scale Ethical AI principles across enterprises, creating safe, secure, and positive outcomes for everyone”",
    "For Organizations: Gain direct access to a core group of leading companies and researchers. Stop guessing how to interpret AI regulations and start implementing proven, peer-reviewed governance frameworks.",
    "For Digital & Legal Leaders: Meet, learn, and share experiences with specialist audiences. Enable yourself to develop actionable methodologies that protect your company from risk while fostering innovation and business resilience.",
    "To maintain the high quality of our network, we operate under strict shared values:",
    "A safe space for data",
    "Members must anonymize all examples, logs, and screenshots before sharing. We use secure, dedicated platforms for collaboration.",
    "Education &compliance first",
    "Focus on sharing informative, regulatory, and technical content.",
    "Non-commercial",
    "This is a dedicated space for peer-to-peer knowledge sharing and problem-solving, free from sales pitches or promotional content.",
    "Inclusive collaboration",
    "We respect differing opinions and promote a positive, cross-industry environment.",
    "Be part of a more responsible digital future!",
    "Engage with professionals to exchange knowledge and insights on Ethical AI, including legal compliance, transparent algorithms, and AI governance. Have questions about joining, our quarterly meetings, or our current workstreams? Reach out to our experts through the contact form to get involved or follow the User Group's progress or to subscribe to the User Group’s monthly Newsletter.",
    "Responsible innovation requires a holistic approach. Discover how Reply is driving sustainability and governance across all digital frontiers:"
  ],
